To place a clickable SVG icon (like a reading glass icon) to the right side of an input field and have it trigger a function when clicked, you can use HTML and JavaScript. Here's a simple example using inline SVG:

### ✅ HTML + JavaScript Example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Search Input with Icon</title>
  <style>
    .search-container {
      position: relative;
      display: inline-block;
    }

    .search-input {
      padding-right: 30px; /* Make space for the icon */
    }

    .search-icon {
      position: absolute;
      right: 5px;
      top: 50%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      cursor: pointer;
      width: 20px;
      height: 20px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="search-container">
    <input type="text" class="search-input" id="searchInput" placeholder="Search..." />
    <svg class="search-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
      <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8"></circle>
      <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <script>
    document.querySelector('.search-icon').addEventListener('click', function() {
      const query = document.getElementById('searchInput').value;
      console.log('Search query:', query);
      // Call your function here, e.g., performSearch(query);
    });
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

---

### 🔍 Explanation

- **`.search-container`**: A container to position the input and icon.
- **`.search-input`**: The input field with padding to avoid text overlapping the icon.
- **`.search-icon`**: The SVG icon positioned absolutely to the right of the input.
- **`addEventListener('click', ...)`**: Adds a click handler to the icon that reads the input value and logs it (or calls a function).

---

### ⚠️ Safety Note

- Make sure the function you call (e.g., `performSearch`) is defined and safe to execute.
- Avoid using inline JavaScript (`onclick`) for better separation of concerns and maintainability.
- If you're using a framework (like React, Vue, etc.), the approach will differ slightly, and I can help with that too.

Let me know if you want a version using a framework or a different icon!
